      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We studied the in-hospital outcome of 138 consecutive patients who received abciximab as a \"rescue\" intervention for complicated coronary angioplasty in a high-risk clinical setting. \"Rescue\" treatment with abciximab was associated with clinical and angiographic success rates of 83% and 84%, respectively, whereas the risk of bleeding was higher in patients of low body weight."},
